  "program": {
    "source": "const A=3,C=1,K=0.5,R=0.12,HALF=2,LIM=8,N=40,S=2,AS=2,START=[1,1.6];\nconst loss=(x,z)=>0.5*(A*x*x+C*z*z);\nconst rand=(n,sd)=>{const v=Math.sin(n*12.9898+sd*78.233+1.7)*43758.5453;return v-Math.floor(v);};\nconst gauss=(n,sd)=>Math.sqrt(-2*Math.log(Math.max(1e-9,rand(n,sd))))*Math.cos(2*Math.PI*rand(n+0.37,sd));\nconst sdOf=b=>b>=64?0:S*Math.sqrt((64-b)/(63*b));\nfunction steps(s,inp,seed){const lr=inp.learningRate,sd=sdOf(Number(inp.batchSize)),k=s.run*997+s.step*2+1,gx=A*s.x,gz=C*s.z;\nreturn{t:[-lr*gx,-lr*gz],m:[-lr*(gx+sd*gauss(k,seed)),-lr*(gz+sd*gauss(k+0.5,seed))]};}\nconst bad=s=>Math.abs(s.x)>HALF||Math.abs(s.z)>HALF||loss(s.x,s.z)>LIM;\nconst word=s=>bad(s)?'diverged':s.step>=N?'finished':'running';\nfunction advance(s,inp,seed){if(word(s)!=='running')return s;const m=steps(s,inp,seed).m,x=s.x+m[0],z=s.z+m[1];\nreturn{...s,x,z,step:s.step+1,path:s.path.concat([[x,z]])};}\nconst fresh=(run,kept)=>({x:START[0],z:START[1],step:0,run,path:[START],kept});\nexport function initialState(){return fresh(0,[]);}\nexport function reduce({state:s,event:e,inputs,seed}){\nif(e.type==='step')return e.tick%4?s:advance(s,inputs,seed);\nif(e.type==='action'&&e.action==='newRun')return fresh(s.run+1,s.step>0?s.path:s.kept);\nreturn s;}\nconst lift=p=>[p[0],Math.min(K*loss(p[0],p[1]),4)+0.05,p[1]];\nfunction aim(d,shown){const l=Math.hypot(d[0],d[1])*AS,h=Math.SQRT1_2;\nreturn shown&&l>1e-6?{visible:true,quaternion:[d[1]*AS/l*h,0,-d[0]*AS/l*h,h],scale:[1,l,1]}:{visible:false};}\nexport function evaluate({inputs,state,seed}){\nconst s=state||initialState(),L=loss(s.x,s.z),live=word(s)==='running',g=steps(s,inputs,seed||7);\nconst gx=K*A*s.x,gz=K*C*s.z;\nreturn{nodes:{ball:{position:[s.x,K*L+R*Math.sqrt(1+gx*gx+gz*gz),s.z]},\nstepArrow:aim(g.m,live),trueArrow:aim(g.t,live&&inputs.showTrueGradient),\ntrail:{points:s.path.map(lift)},ghost:{points:s.kept.map(lift)}},\nreadouts:{steps:s.step,loss:L,stepLen:Math.hypot(g.m[0],g.m[1]),status:word(s)}};}\n"
  },
  "assumptions": [
    "Illustration: a made-up two-setting loss bowl with simulated batch noise, not a real model trained on real data.",
    "Loss = (3x² + z²)/2, drawn at half its value as a surface with contours. It is 3 times steeper along x, so overshoot appears there first: steps along x grow once the learning rate passes 2/3.",
    "Each update moves the ball by −learning rate × (true slope + noise). The noise has standard deviation 2·√((64−b)/(63b)) per axis for batch size b: largest at b = 1, exactly zero at 64. It lowers the loss only on average.",
    "Both arrows are drawn at 2 times the step they show: orange is the mini-batch step the ball will take, grey is −learning rate × full-data slope. The step-length readout is the true length, in bowl units.",
    "A run stops after 40 updates (finished), or diverges if the ball leaves the drawn square or the loss passes 8, the bowl's corner height. A diverged ball is held at the bowl's rim on screen; the loss readout keeps its true value.",
    "The ball takes one update every 4 host ticks (about 7.5 a second). The trail holds the start plus up to 40 landing points; the ghost holds the last finished path.",
    "Noise comes from a fixed seed. Reset replays the same sequence. 'New run, keep last path' moves on to the next noise values.",
    "Changing a setting mid-run affects the next updates only; earlier steps stay as they were."
  ]
}